  <question type="essay">
    <name><text>M11 - Proof by contradiction: irrational minus rational</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>[Proof — Contradiction]</strong> Prove by contradiction that the difference of an irrational number and a rational number is irrational. Hint: let x be irrational and r rational, and suppose x - r is rational.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Model proof.</strong> Suppose x - r = d is rational. Then x = d + r is a sum of two rationals, hence rational — contradicting that x is irrational. Therefore x - r is irrational.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <responseformat>editor</responseformat>
    <responserequired>1</responserequired>
    <responsefieldlines>12</responsefieldlines>
    <attachments>0</attachments>
    <attachmentsrequired>0</attachmentsrequired>
    <graderinfo format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Credit for assuming x-r rational, writing x=(x-r)+r, noting sum of rationals is rational, and concluding.</p>]]></text></graderinfo>
    <responsetemplate format="html"><text></text></responsetemplate>
  </question>

  <question type="essay">
    <name><text>M12 - Proof by contraposition: 7n+4 odd implies n odd</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>[Proof — Contraposition]</strong> Let n be an integer. Prove that if 7n + 4 is odd then n is odd, using contraposition.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Model proof.</strong> Contrapositive: if n is even then 7n+4 is even. If n = 2k then 7n+4 = 14k+4 = 2(7k+2), which is even. Hence the original statement holds.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <responseformat>editor</responseformat>
    <responserequired>1</responserequired>
    <responsefieldlines>12</responsefieldlines>
    <attachments>0</attachments>
    <attachmentsrequired>0</attachmentsrequired>
    <graderinfo format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Credit for stating the contrapositive, writing n=2k, showing 7n+4=2m, and concluding.</p>]]></text></graderinfo>
    <responsetemplate format="html"><text></text></responsetemplate>
  </question>

